  "note": "The room is in development: Decide what the book is: the Director writes the brief and settles the world, then the Plotter and the Character Designer work at the same time on the plot and the people, and the Continuity Editor checks the four files agree.\n\ndraft.md is the showrunner's own draft of the book. It is not finished and it is not binding, but it is the book they mean to make: plan around what it does - its scenes, its order, its people - and improve on it, rather than planning a different book. Where the pre-production files and the draft disagree, the files win, and say so in your notes.",
